error[NK1302]: `names[at]` is not proved in bounds, and `at` comes from outside the program.
   --> tests/outside_data_through_a_result_and_a_field.nika:30:2
    |
 30 | 	println(names[at])
    |  ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^
    |
    = note: `at` comes from `io::read_to_string`: whoever sends it chooses the value, so nothing the compiler can see says what it holds.
    = note: What is known here does not exclude `at` can be -1, `names.len()` can be 3, for which `0 <= at < names.len()` fails.
    = help: Check it where it arrives, with a guard the program handles: `throw BadInput(at) if !(0 <= at && at < names.len())`, or the early `return` that rejects it. After that line, the index is proved.
